{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgk7a238c7SUo4AtV82MR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "If UserService goes down, **6 services** are affected within two hops.\n\n**Hop 1: services that depend directly on UserService**\n1. **ApiGateway**: ApiGateway \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService\n2. **AuditService**: AuditService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService\n3. **OrderService**: OrderService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService\n\n**Hop 2: services that depend on a hop-1 service or call its API**\n4. **BillingService**: BillingService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 OrderService \u2192 UserService\n5. **ReportingService**: ReportingService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 OrderService \u2192 UserService\n6. **SearchService**: SearchService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 OrderService \u2192 UserService\n\n**Other points:**\n- Every link from UserService is a DEPENDS_ON relationship. The graph search found no service that calls a UserService API.\n- ApiGateway also calls **OrdersAPI**, the API that OrderService exposes. That gives it a second path to UserService, but it's already counted in hop 1.\n- Nothing depends on **ApiGateway** or **AuditService**, so all of hop 2 comes through **OrderService**. That makes OrderService the main way a UserService outage spreads.\n- No databases or configuration keys are part of these paths."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 255, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5026, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 255}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "9d68e1d2-fc07-4eba-bd5d-55118fd1b153", "uuid": "0410866f-e578-49a2-a9e9-87a918ca0db0", "time